# Supabase credentials — required by scripts/seed-auth-users.mjs and the future
# app (W3+, which uses @supabase/server).
#
# Naming follows Supabase's current convention (the @supabase/server package).
# The older "anon / service_role" naming still works at the API level but the
# new names are clearer about what each key does.
#
# DO NOT COMMIT your real .env. This file is .gitignored (see Jayshankar/.gitignore).
# Copy this file to scripts/.env and fill in the values.
#
# Where to find these:
#   1. Go to https://supabase.com/dashboard
#   2. Open your project
#   3. Project Settings → API Keys (the new panel; "Legacy" tab has the old names)
#   4. Copy "Project URL" → SUPABASE_URL
#   5. Copy "Publishable key" → SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#   6. Copy "Secret key" → SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
#   7. Copy the "JWT Secret Key" JWKS URL (or set it to https://<ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/jwks) → SUPABASE_JWKS_URL
#
# SECURITY:
#   - SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the one that ships in the browser bundle (RLS-enforced).
#   - SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY bypasses RLS — server-only, never commit, never log.
#     scripts/seed-auth-users.mjs uses it to call the Admin API (which is server-side
#     by definition).
#   - SUPABASE_JWKS_URL is for JWT verification by @supabase/server (future app). Not
#     needed by the seed script.

# Demo user passwords. Defaults to "DevPassword123!" if unset.
# Use strong passwords in production; these defaults are for the gatekeeper demo.
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!
SEED_REP_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!
SEED_WORKER_PASSWORD=DevPassword123!
